I can't tell the features apart: they have no names or descriptions, so I have no domain basis to rank them. This looks like the eye-tracking benchmark from the PROMISE/"Eye movements" (OpenML, 2005 data) set. Its columns are usually line number, word number, and various fixation and regression measures, but I can't map those to the indices here.

With nothing to go on, I give every feature a similar prior of about 0.3. The only variation I add is a slight upward tilt for the middle and later indices, which in the original dataset tend to be fixation-duration and regression measures. That tilt is a guess, not evidence.

